     "page": 1,
     "text": "**CERTIFIED TRANSLATION - original in Hindi**\n\n**Translator**: A. Santos, cert #51095\n\n**Patient**: Katie Sampson\n- **DOB**: 15/10/1g51\n- **Sex**: Female\n\n---\n\n**Attending Physician Statement**\n\n**Dr. Daniel Lee**\n\n**Family Medicine**\n\n**Leonard PLC Clinic**\n\n---\n\n**Medical Record Summary**\n\n**Patient**: Katie Sampson\n\n---\n\n**Medical History**\n\nKatie Sampson, a 74-year-old female, presents with a history of concussion/traumatic brain injury (TBI) since June 10, 2016. The patient has been under continuous follow-up for this condition. Additionally, she has a controlled gout condition, which began on April 23, 2018. Katie has been prescribed colchicine 0.6 mg for the management of her gout.\n\n**Family History**\n\nKatie's mother had a history of hypertension, which began at the age of 79 and in her passing at the age of 83. Katie's mother is deceased.\n\n---\n\n**Clinical Visits**\n\n1. **Visit Date**: 13/02/2026\n - **Reason for Visit**: Follow-up for concussion/TBI.\n - **Blood Pressure**: 151/74 mmHg\n - **Weight**: 145 lb\n - **Exam Findings**: The patient reports no residual symptoms related to her concussion. General physical examination, including neurological assessment, is within normal limits. No acute distress observed.\n\n2. **Visit Date**: 26/04/2025\n - **Reason for Visit**: Follow-up for concussion/TBI.\n - **Blood Pressure**: 139/85 mmHg\n **Weight**: 156 lb\n - **Exam Findings**: The patient continues to have no residual symptoms from her TBI. Musculoskeletal examination is unremarkable. Cardiovascular and respiratory assessments are normal.\n\n3. **Visit Date**: 06/07/2024\n - **Reason for Visit**: Follow-up for concussion/TBI.\n - **Blood Pressure**: 148/76 mmHg\n - **Weight**: 149 lb\n - **Exam Findings**: No new symptoms related to her TBI were reported. Neurological examination is stable. Cardiovascular and respiratory systems are normal. There are no signs of gout flare-up.\n\n4. **Visit Date**: 16/09/2023\n - **Reason for Visit**: Follow-up for gout.\n - **Blood Pressure**: 149/83 mmHg\n - **Weight**: 150 lb\n - **Exam Findings**: The patient has no gout symptoms at the moment. General physical examination, including the joints, is normal. Cardiovascular and respiratory systems are also normal.\n\n5. **Visit Date**: 26/11/2022\n - **Reason for Visit**: Follow-up for gout.\n - **Blood Pressure**: 139/77 mmHg\n - **Weight**: lb\n - **Exam Findings**: The patient is doing well with her gout management. There are no signs of acute gout flare. General physical examination is unremarkable. Cardiovascular and respiratory"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "examinations are normal.\n\n---\n\n**Lifestyle and Social History**\n\nKatie Sampson reports engaging in regular physical activity, running 3-4 times a week. She consumes approximately 10 alcoholic drinks per week. There are no reported issues with tobacco use.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nKatie Sampson's concussion/TBI and gout are currently under control with no residual symptoms. Her management plan includes colchicine 0.6 mg for gout. She maintains a healthy lifestyle with regular exercise and moderate alcohol consumption. The patient's cardiovascular and musculoskeletal examinations are within normal limits.\n\n---\n\n**Translator's Note**\n\nThis translation has been certified to be an representation of the original medical records in Hindi. All clinical findings, diagnoses, and treatment plans are faithfully represented as per the original documents.\n"
